<title>USA: WHX says Dynamics concedes on WHX-Warren Group.</title>
<headline>WHX says Dynamics concedes on WHX-Warren Group.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>WHX Corp said Thursday Dynamics Corp of America has conceded as &quot;immaterial&quot; the issue of whether or not it has formed an illegal and undisclosed 13D group with Warren Lichtenstein and Steel Partners.</p>
<p>The company said a trial on the issue was orginally scheduled for May 5, but Dynamics has requested an indefinite adjournment on the issue. The company said Dynmanics requested the adjournment since is is not material to WHX's amended tender offer for shares of Dynamics at $45 per share.</p>
<p>The company said the court granted this request.</p>
</text>
